{"should_block? does a non-atomic read-modify-write (match_count += 1 then save) which can lose increments under concurrent calls, and ignores failed saves so stats updates can silently be dropped": 0.8994768857955933, "Email comparisons in should_block? use exact lookup, but email comparisons elsewhere normalize via Email.downcase/strip, so case/whitespace variations can bypass a blocked entry. Should normalize the input": 0.9065573215484619, "validate_each calls email_in_restriction_setting? and BlockedEmail.should_block? even when value is blank/nil, which can raise errors (e.g., nil =~ regexp). Should guard early with return if value.blank?": 0.8054215312004089, "The model sets a default action_type in a callback, but the DB column has no default. Adding a database default would make manual/bulk inserts safer and align with the model's behavior": 0.6966252326965332, "rejectedEmails: Em.A([]) creates a mutable array on the controller prototype that can unintentionally persist across controller reuse. Should initialize it per-instance in init": 0.47742927074432373, "The computed property depends on rejectedEmails contents but uses rejectedEmails.@each which is for observing property changes on array items. Should use rejectedEmails.[] to reliably recompute when items are added/removed": 0.8809309005737305, "The create endpoint now returns errors and values keys on failure, but there are no controller specs asserting this new response shape, so regressions could slip in": 0.2561261057853699, "Should use atomic UPDATE ... match_count = match_count + 1 (e.g., update_all) for the stats update instead of read-modify-write": 0.867203414440155}